# Agent product context

- Read and follow root `AGENTS.md` (global: challenge, jury profiling, rules), then `agents/<role>/AGENTS.md`.
- Check `comms/` inboxes relevant to your role every turn.
- Stay aligned with the official NASA challenge: interactive NISAR SAR surface-change visualization for a broad audience; default AOI is Santiago del Estero, fully config-driven for any location.
- Design the globe + side controls, layers-by-job, and portable NISAR pipeline so the product stands on its own for the jury archetypes listed in `AGENTS.md` — without naming them in the UI.
- User-facing copy: humanizer ES-AR-SGO only.
- `references/` is code-drop only (SgoLinea, gods-eye-view). Do not put agent docs there.
- Never put into the UI (or end-user README/demo overlays) any mention of juries, evaluators, hackathon scoring, or that features exist to impress a panel. No “diseñado para ingenieros/científicos/gobierno” style audience-bait in visible strings.
